    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71498407\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\" itemprop=\"articleBody\"><p>There is something amusing about the fact that a city famous for Chinese fishing nets, churches, synagogues and the occasional wholesome family lunch is also becoming a surprisingly interesting place to talk about sex.</p><p>In Kochi, the conversation is increasingly moving beyond the old binary of sex as either something that happens after marriage or something that happens in whispers. Dating apps have given young Malayalis a new vocabulary for meeting people; words such as “breadcrumbing”, “ghosting” and “situationship” have entered the local lexicon, while platforms built specifically around Malayali identity are offering an alternative to the generic swipe.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- September 26, 2026 07:00 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71498407\" data-title=\"Kochi Is changing the way it dates, talks about sex and relationships\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/columns/kochi-is-changing-the-way-it-dates-talks-about-sex-and-relationships/article71498407.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-2e2dad7462a101effea79067-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/columns/kochi-is-changing-the-way-it-dates-talks-about-sex-and-relationships/article71498407.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=Kochi%20Is%20changi